			<div class="p-3">
				<h3 class="m-0">Sorting Algorithm Visualizer</h3>
				<p class="m-0">
					A tool for visualizing 11+ sorting algorithms. Although other tools for this already exist, I wanted to build one that would work on the web and visualize auxiliary memory.
				</p>
			</div>
		</helion-card>-->
	</helion-wrapping-grid>
</section>

<section data-category="heledron">
	<h2>Minecraft Modding</h2>
	<p>
		I worked on a few Minecraft programming projects with companion YouTube tutorials.
	</p>
	<helion-wrapping-grid style="--min-column-width: 300px; gap: 1.5rem;" class="print:text-sm">
		<a class="helion-card overflow-hidden text-inherit! no-underline!" href="https://youtu.be/PSnPOYeTW-0" target="_blank">
			<img class="w-full block" width="1280" height="720" src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/PSnPOYeTW-0/maxresdefault.jpg" alt="Procedurally Animated Robots in Minecraft" />
			<div class="p-3">
				Procedurally Animated Robots in Minecraft
			</div>
		</a>
		<a class="helion-card overflow-hidden text-inherit! no-underline!" href="https://youtu.be/RnLWLQsh9mw" target="_blank">
			<img class="w-full block" width="1280" height="720" src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/RnLWLQsh9mw/maxresdefault.jpg" alt="3D Meshes with Text Displays in Minecraft" />
			<div class="p-3">
				3D Meshes with Text Displays in Minecraft
			</div>
		</a>
		<a class="helion-card overflow-hidden text-inherit! no-underline!" href="https://youtu.be/dr83cXTESXY" target="_blank">
			<img class="w-full block" width="1280" height="720" src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/dr83cXTESXY/maxresdefault.jpg" alt="3D Renderer in Minecraft" />
			<div class="p-3">
				A working animated 3D Rendering Pipeline in Minecraft
			</div>
		</a>
		<a class="helion-card overflow-hidden text-inherit! no-underline!" href="https://youtu.be/aLR4YpTnM6c" target="_blank">
			<img class="w-full block" width="1280" height="720" src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/aLR4YpTnM6c/maxresdefault.jpg" alt="6 Dimensional Mandelbrot in Minecraft" />
			<div class="p-3">
				6 Dimensional Mandelbrot in Minecraft
			</div>
		</a>
	</helion-wrapping-grid>

	<br>

	<p>
		I also worked with the design studio <a href="https://varunabuilds.com/" target="_blank">Varuna</a>. I was the sole programmer for
		<a href="https://headlinermagazine.net/alfie-templeman-celebrates-new-album-launch-with-virtual-minecraft-festival.html" target="_blank">The Alfie Templeman Minecraft Festival</a> and <a href="https://varunabuilds.com/nijisanji-prism-cup" target="_blank">Nijisanji Prism Cup 2023</a>.
	</p>
</section>

<section data-category="heledron">
	<h2>ECS Game Engine</h2>
	<div
		class="grid gap-4"
		style={`grid-template-columns: minmax(0, ${PhysicsEngine.width / PhysicsEngine.height}fr) minmax(0, ${IKSystem.width / IKSystem.height}fr);`}
	>
		<Image class="shadow-md w-full max-w-100" src={PhysicsEngine} alt="ECS Physics Engine" />
		<Image class="shadow-md w-full max-w-100" src={IKSystem} alt="ECS IK System" />
	</div>

	<p>
		A work-in-progress ECS game engine inspired by Bevy. It currently features a 2D physics engine, a tilemap system, a rudimentary 3D renderer, and an IK system.
	</p>
</section>

<section data-category="heledron">
	<h2>Legacy Game Engine</h2>
	<div
		class="grid gap-4 max-w-200"
		style={`grid-template-columns: minmax(0, ${GameEngine2DShooter.width / GameEngine2DShooter.height}fr) minmax(0, ${GameEngineDeep.width / GameEngineDeep.height}fr);`}
	>
		<Image class="shadow-md" src={GameEngine2DShooter} alt="Legacy Game Engine" />
		<Image class="shadow-md nearest-neighbor" src={GameEngineDeep} alt="Legacy Game Engine" />
	</div>

	<p>
		A 2D game engine I built when I was a beginner, which I used to make a few games. It was abandoned in favour of the ECS engine.
	</p>
</section>

<section data-category="heledron">
	<h2>ICECube (Code Editor)</h2>
	<Image src={ICECube} alt="ICECube IDE" class="block shadow-md max-h-70 w-auto mb-5" />

	<p>
		This was my first major project, a code editor for both web and desktop.
	</p>
	
	<p>
		It featured a code editor with syntax highlighting, a JSON editor capable of editing complex nested JSON objects defined by schemas, and multiple graphical editors, all built from scratch.
	</p>

	<p>
		It was abandoned due to a lack of users, and my improved standards for code quality and UX.
	</p>
</section>